-- title:
--   Complex conjugation generates decomposition groups at infinite places
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ (inside Mathlib's `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) which is a number field, Galois over $\mathbb Q$, and totally complex, and let $w$ be an infinite place of $F$. Write $c =$ [`complexConjugation`](def/GaloisRep_ComplexConjugation.html#L30) for the automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\mathbb Q$ obtained by restricting to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism of $\mathbb C$ given by complex conjugation, and write $\pi_F$ for `AlgEquiv.restrictNormalHom`, the restriction homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q) \to F \simeq_{\mathbb Q} F$. The assertion is that there exists $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ such that, setting $c_\sigma = \pi_F(\sigma^{-1} c\, \sigma)$: (i) $c_\sigma$ lies in `decomp ℚ F w`, which by definition is the stabiliser of $w$ for the action of the group $F \simeq_{\mathbb Q} F$ on the infinite places of $F$; (ii) $c_\sigma \neq 1$; (iii) every element $d$ of that stabiliser satisfies $d = 1$ or $d = c_\sigma$; and (iv) $\sigma^{-1} c\, \sigma$ does not lie in `F.fixingSubgroup`, i.e. it does not act as the identity on $F$. Thus the decomposition group of $w$ in $\mathrm{Gal}(F/\mathbb Q)$ is the two-element group generated by a conjugate of complex conjugation.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic description of the decomposition group at an archimedean place of a totally complex Galois number field: it has order $2$ and is generated by a conjugate of complex conjugation, realised through a fixed embedding of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ into $\mathbb C$. It supplies the archimedean input for the local terms in the Poitou–Tate style computations, being cited in the construction of the archimedean local restriction classes and in the nondegeneracy of the Šafarevič–Tate pairing away from $p = 2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_InfPlaceDecomp_exists_restrictNormalHom_conj_complexConjugation_mem_decomp.lean

